  "implementation": "One C TCP implementation shared by standalone archives and legacy imports. Canonical records retain visible layouts and fields; private allocation prefixes distinguish factory-owned resources from zero/default records. Atomic credits close factory resources on last release, preserve aliases and permit idempotent explicit disposal. WinSock initialization is serialized. Peer disconnects use per-send/per-socket SIGPIPE prevention, without changing process signal disposition.",
  "independent_controls": "C/Rust archive clients cover all15 raw entrypoints, live aliases, owned snapshots after owner release, binary/NUL/high bytes, line/buffer reads, EOF, timeouts, disposal, zero/default/nil states, stdin preservation, repeated loopback and parallel independent factories. The checker includes platform socket/descriptor closure checks, a portable readable-socket shutdown test and a POSIX default-SIGPIPE child test. Generated legacy C is independently compared with canonical storage for sizes, alignments and all field offsets/widths.",
